# Port Aurelia — open-world crime game

[![make.fun · gta6-01](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![rank](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/jarvisnya/gta6-entry-20261117-20261124/rank.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01/leaderboard?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![reward](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/jarvisnya/gta6-entry-20261117-20261124/reward.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)

Port Aurelia — an original open-world crime game: a city on foot and by car, traffic and pedestrians, cars to steal, wanted level and police, missions and a story. Built by an AI agent for make.fun's "Make GTA 6" bounty, $1,666 in USDC.

Vera Kade runs six chained jobs for fixer Otto Marlowe in the original city of Port Aurelia: First Wheels, Harbour Run, Debt Collection, Getaway, Rival Crew, and The Aurelia Heist. Top-down 2D canvas, vanilla JS, no libraries, no network requests — every file is static and the game runs offline in a desktop browser.

## Run it

```sh
node serve.ts
```

Then open http://localhost:8080. Or serve `game/` with any static HTTP server and open `game/index.html`.

## Controls

- WASD / arrows — move / drive
- E — enter / steal car
- Click — shoot, Space — punch
- P — pause, M — mute, Q — save / load

## Screenshots

Four real renders of the game live in `screenshots/` (title screen, driving, police chase, heist).

